  "nl_text": "This schema, named schemabench_0118, contains three tables: country, relation, and stat.\nThe country table has two columns: country_id and country. The country_id column is an integer and is the primary key, while the country column is a string. The country table also has a foreign key constraint that references the stat table.\nThe relation table has four columns: nation_id1, nation_id2, relation, and value. The nation_id1 and nation_id2 columns are both integers and are the primary key. The relation column is a string, and the value column is an integer. The relation table also has foreign key constraints that reference the country table.\nThe stat table has 52 columns, including country_id, which is an integer and is the primary key. The remaining columns are all integers, with the exception of country, which is a string. The stat table also has foreign key constraints that reference the country table.\nIn summary, this schema contains three tables: country, relation, and stat. The country table has two columns, while the relation table has four columns. The stat table has 52 columns, including a primary key. The schema also has foreign key constraints that reference the country table.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context  \nThe project involves developing a database system to store and analyze data related to global national statistics and relationships between countries. This system is part of a larger effort to enhance data-driven decision-making and policy analysis.\n\n2) Objectives  \nThe primary objective is to create a relational database that can manage and query data about countries, their bilateral relations, and various socio-economic and political statistics. The system aims to facilitate comprehensive analysis and reporting on international indicators.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users  \n- Stakeholders:  \n  - International Policy Analysts  \n  - Researchers in Political Science and Economics  \n  - Government Agencies  \n  - Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs)  \n\n- Users:  \n  - Data Scientists  \n  - Policy Makers  \n  - Academic Researchers\n\n4) Functional Descriptions  \n- Database Management:  \n  The system will manage records for countries, including their ID and name.\n  \n- Relation Tracking:  \n  Facilitate storage and retrieval of relationships between countries with associated values like economic, political, and military ties.\n\n- Statistical Analysis:  \n  Maintain a wide range of statistics per country, such as population, economic indicators (e.g., GNP, exports/imports), social indicators (e.g., literacy, unemployment), and political metrics.\n\n- Reporting and Querying:  \n  Enable users to perform complex queries to generate customized reports analyzing international trends and relationships.\n\n- Data Integrity:  \n  Ensure data consistency and integrity through foreign key relationships and constraints.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions  \n- Scalability:  \n  The system should efficiently handle a growing amount of data as more countries and statistics are included.\n\n- Performance:  \n  Queries should return results within an acceptable timeframe to ensure efficient data analysis.\n\n- Security:  \n  Protect sensitive statistical data from unauthorized access and ensure compliance with data protection regulations.\n\n- Reliability:  \n  The system should provide reliable access to data without significant downtime.\n\n- Maintenance:  \n  The database system should support easy maintenance and upgrades without disrupting analytical processes.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0118.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0118\nCREATE TABLE `country` (\n  `country_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `country_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`country_id`) REFERENCES `stat` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `relation` (\n  `nation_id1` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `nation_id2` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `relation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`nation_id1`, `nation_id2`),\n  CONSTRAINT `relation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`nation_id1`) REFERENCES `country` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `relation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`nation_id2`) REFERENCES `country` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stat` (\n  `country_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_1` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_2` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_3` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_4` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_5` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_6` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_7` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_8` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_9` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_10` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_11` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_12` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_13` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_14` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_15` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_16` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_17` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_18` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_19` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_20` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_21` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_22` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_23` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_24` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_25` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_26` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_27` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_28` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_29` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_30` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_31` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_32` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_33` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_34` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_35` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_36` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_37` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_38` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_39` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_40` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_41` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_42` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_43` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_44` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_45` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_46` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_47` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_48` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_49` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_50` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_51` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stat_col_52` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stat_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`country_id`) REFERENCES `country` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
